RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4122619Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4133071Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4234761Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4244917Z ^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4246405Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4246884Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4247092Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4247460Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4248349Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4248657Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4248827Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4249179Z    if you are ready to continue.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4249346Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4249722Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4250242Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4250654Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4250977Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4251127Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4251284Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4251530Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4251708Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4252060Z    can use Nix.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4252191Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4252277Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4252430Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4252775Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4253230Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4258283Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4258541Z I will:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4258668Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4258848Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4259368Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4260093Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4260716Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4261009Z  - install Nix in /nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4261277Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4261667Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4262020Z    /root
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4274801Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4275629Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4286564Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4287091Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4287493Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4289182Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4289783Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4307668Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4308419Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4318377Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4319014Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4319702Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4320041Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4320296Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4320754Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4321062Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4321748Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T15:11:36.4322135Z 
